sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as API caller
    participant D as Django
    participant S as Transactional sends
    participant K as Idempotency keys
    participant J as Adapter, manager
    participant T as Run history, status rows
    participant W as Worker
    C->>D: POST send/email, scheduled_at, Idempotency-Key
    Note right of D: flag gates, send throttles,<br/>parse scheduled_at
    D->>S: send route, JWT team + workflow
    S->>K: reserve(key, fingerprint)
    alt key already queued
        K-->>S: first message id, accepted time
        opt the accepted time is set
            S->>T: status row scheduled again
        end
        S-->>C: 202 as first answered, replayed
    else key reserved
        Note right of S: time rules: at or before now is a send now,<br/>after created + 30 days is 400 too_far.<br/>Then the refusal checks.
        alt a rule or a check fails
            S->>K: release(key)
            S-->>C: 4xx
        else all pass
            S->>T: run row running
            S->>J: queueInvocations, scheduled = send time
            Note right of J: email queue, available,<br/>transition_count 0
            S->>K: markQueued with the accepted time
            S->>T: status row scheduled or queued, flush
            S-->>C: 202 scheduled or queued, message_id
        end
    end
    Note over J,W: waits until scheduled <= now
    W->>J: fairDequeueJobs, SKIP LOCKED
    Note right of J: running, transition_count 1
    Note left of W: send-time checks: workflow active,<br/>suspended, paused, suppressed, sender
    W->>T: sent, or failed with a reason
